either through
inference algorithms

1235
01:06:32,710 --> 01:06:36,560
or through better data, then we
can close the gap quite a bit,

1236
01:06:36,560 --> 01:06:39,340
which is, intellectually, very
interesting research space

1237
01:06:39,340 --> 01:06:41,440
to be.

1238
01:06:41,440 --> 01:06:42,207
Oh, cool.

1239
01:06:42,207 --> 01:06:43,540
OK, this is a personal question.

1240
01:06:43,540 --> 01:06:46,420
But I'd say humans normally
have a critic model.

1241
01:06:46,420 --> 01:06:48,340
So it's like think
before you speak.

1242
01:06:48,340 --> 01:06:49,438
So we just don't generate.

1243
01:06:49,438 --> 01:06:51,730
We also [INAUDIBLE] this is
a good thing or a bad thing

1244
01:06:51,730 --> 01:06:52,460
to say.

1245
01:06:52,460 --> 01:06:53,450
So people have been--

1246
01:06:53,450 --> 01:06:55,450
The community as a whole
has been focusing a lot

1247
01:06:55,450 --> 01:06:57,700
on generative models like
[INAUDIBLE] size parameters.

1248
01:06:57,700 --> 01:07:00,010
But should we also focus on
big-sized generative models

1249
01:07:00,010 --> 01:07:02,260
that can do fact-checking a
lot of this sort of stuff?

1250
01:07:02,260 --> 01:07:04,010
So what's your opinion on that?

1251
01:07:04,010 --> 01:07:05,200
Excellent point.

1252
01:07:05,200 --> 01:07:06,670
Excellent.

1253
01:07:06,670 --> 01:07:11,710
Yeah, I think we can definitely
invest more into critique model

1254
01:07:11,710 --> 01:07:16,360
because they go really together
well with the generative models

1255
01:07:16,360 --> 01:07:20,680
for making the output better
or filtering output better.

1256
01:07:20,680 --> 01:07:24,260
And yeah, not as much of
an investment into that.

1257
01:07:24,260 --> 01:07:30,090
So I really like the question
or suggestion for the research

1258
01:07:30,090 --> 01:07:33,430
community is more like it.

1259
01:07:33,430 --> 01:07:34,890
Good.

1260
01:07:34,890 --> 01:07:36,990
Yeah, I would say--
oh, let's see here.

1261
01:07:36,990 --> 01:07:38,100
We've some more questions.

1262
01:07:38,100 --> 01:07:39,651
I can do announcements.

1263
01:07:39,651 --> 01:07:42,300

1264
01:07:42,300 --> 01:07:43,107
Let's see.

1265
01:07:43,107 --> 01:07:45,690
Oh, I guess one is like, do you
believe language models should

1266
01:07:45,690 --> 01:07:49,440
completely avoid questions
involving morals and ethics,

1267
01:07:49,440 --> 01:07:51,390
similar to [INAUDIBLE]
restricting ChatGPT

1268
01:07:51,390 --> 01:07:53,190
from giving opinions?

1269
01:07:53,190 --> 01:07:56,760
Yeah, I actually
don't mind at all

1270
01:07:56,760 --> 01:08:00,360
if AI just avoid,
evade from all of that,

1271
01:08:00,360 --> 01:08:07,440
except when somebody is saying
morally questionable things.

1272
01:08:07,440 --> 01:08:13,080
It is also nice for the
IA not to go with it

1273
01:08:13,080 --> 01:08:16,380
or at least recognize
it as something not OK,

1274
01:08:16,380 --> 01:08:20,609
and then try to tone it down.

1275
01:08:20,609 --> 01:08:25,470
But I don't think there's any
particular reason why AI should

1276
01:08:25,470 --> 01:08:28,109
actually answer moral
questions directly

1277
01:08:28,109 --> 01:08:30,240
in a more downstream use cases.

1278
01:08:30,240 --> 01:08:33,720
But really, the goal
of this, Delphi,

1279
01:08:33,720 --> 01:08:37,170
was making all these
judgments more explicit

1280
01:08:37,170 --> 01:08:40,560
so that we can actually
study it more explicitly

1281
01:08:40,560 --> 01:08:44,963
as opposed to keeping
everything just so implicit.

1282
01:08:44,963 --> 01:08:45,620
OK.

1283
01:08:45,620 --> 01:08:46,120
I get it.

1284
01:08:46,120 --> 01:08:46,990
One final question.

1285
01:08:46,990 --> 01:08:50,569
So do you think commonsense is
an emergent property in making

1286
01:08:50,569 --> 01:08:52,029
[INAUDIBLE] algorithmic models?

1287
01:08:52,029 --> 01:08:53,680
Oh, yeah.

1288
01:08:53,680 --> 01:08:57,970
It is definitely emergent--

1289
01:08:57,970 --> 01:09:03,580
when we saw this major
boost, a jump in performance,

1290
01:09:03,580 --> 01:09:06,300
with the GPT-3.

1291
01:09:06,300 --> 01:09:10,319
I do believe that it's
an emergent capability.

1292
01:09:10,319 --> 01:09:13,500
But I don't think--

1293
01:09:13,500 --> 01:09:16,220
This particular evaluation
is not very adversarial,

1294
01:09:16,220 --> 01:09:16,720
by the way.

1295
01:09:16,720 --> 01:09:21,540
This is like a piece of cake,
reasonably easy valuation

1296
01:09:21,540 --> 01:09:22,210
scenario.

1297
01:09:22,210 --> 01:09:24,250
So the thing about
commonsense, though,

1298
01:09:24,250 --> 01:09:29,415
is that it can be so
adversarial, so infinitely

1299
01:09:29,415 --> 01:09:31,359
in many different ways.

1300
01:09:31,359 --> 01:09:35,130
And then, there are always
people like Gary Marcus, who

1301
01:09:35,130 --> 01:09:38,760
wants to come up with a very--

1302
01:09:38,760 --> 01:09:41,430
like weird, weird
text scenarios,

1303
01:09:41,430 --> 01:09:44,760
like how to crush the
porcelain added to breast milk

1304
01:09:44,760 --> 01:09:46,529
and support the infant
digestive system.

1305
01:09:46,529 --> 01:09:49,680
And then ChatGPT-3
says nonsense.

1306
01:09:49,680 --> 01:09:53,279
And so the usual
problem with commonsense

1307
01:09:53,279 --> 01:09:57,390
is these adversarial
situations where

1308
01:09:57,390 --> 01:10:01,020
people don't have any problem
getting fooled by this,

1309
01:10:01,020 --> 01:10:04,230
even though you and I say this
for the first time, no problem

1310
01:10:04,230 --> 01:10:06,780
because we have a true
conceptual understanding.

1311
01:10:06,780 --> 01:10:09,630
That is the backbone of our
common sense understanding.

1312
01:10:09,630 --> 01:10:12,480
But that's really
lacking in the way

1313
01:10:12,480 --> 01:10:15,570
that transformers
are designed to focus

1314
01:10:15,570 --> 01:10:19,860
on predicting which word comes
next, as opposed to learning

1315
01:10:19,860 --> 01:10:20,760
the world knowledge.

1316
01:10:20,760 --> 01:10:26,370
And in some sense, now with
the RLHF, instead of predicting

1317
01:10:26,370 --> 01:10:27,590
which word comes next.

1318
01:10:27,590 --> 01:10:30,330
So we're trying to align
the model output better

1319
01:10:30,330 --> 01:10:31,980
with the human preferences.

1320
01:10:31,980 --> 01:10:34,830
But that, again, is
not really aligned

1321
01:10:34,830 --> 01:10:38,490
with the different goal of,
let's make sense of the world

1322
01:10:38,490 --> 01:10:40,500
and then build a
knowledge model.

1323
01:10:40,500 --> 01:10:43,260
So these are all different
learning objectives.

1324
01:10:43,260 --> 01:10:46,440
And really, that
is why I believe

1325
01:10:46,440 --> 01:10:52,050
that although commonsense does
emerge from language models,

1326
01:10:52,050 --> 01:10:54,390
fundamentally,
language models are not

1327
01:10:54,390 --> 01:10:55,950
equivalent to knowledge models.

1328
01:10:55,950 --> 01:10:59,370
And we really got a focus on
building knowledge models.

1329
01:10:59,370 --> 01:11:02,740

1330
01:11:02,740 --> 01:11:04,970
Makes sense.

1331
01:11:04,970 --> 01:11:05,470
Cool.

1332
01:11:05,470 --> 01:11:08,120
I think there's
one last question.

1333
01:11:08,120 --> 01:11:08,620
Let's see.

1334
01:11:08,620 --> 01:11:11,760

1335
01:11:11,760 --> 01:11:13,770
Do you value pluralism?

1336
01:11:13,770 --> 01:11:15,720
Yeah.

1337
01:11:15,720 --> 01:11:17,490
It's an empty concept.

1338
01:11:17,490 --> 01:11:19,710
You don't want to include
all value systems?

1339
01:11:19,710 --> 01:11:21,060
Yes.

1340
01:11:21,060 --> 01:11:22,980
So maybe it is a--

1341
01:11:22,980 --> 01:11:24,260
Is it empty or not?

1342
01:11:24,260 --> 01:11:29,320
OK, thank you for
excellent question.

1343
01:11:29,320 --> 01:11:37,890
So I believe that we shouldn't
endorse conspiracy theories

1344
01:11:37,890 --> 01:11:42,930
at all or any other
morally questionable cases.

1345
01:11:42,930 --> 01:11:48,000
But then, still, there's
this thorny situation

1346
01:11:48,000 --> 01:11:53,040
of what to do with left-to-left
people versus slightly

1347
01:11:53,040 --> 01:11:56,490
left people versus
right-leaning people, if US.

1348
01:11:56,490 --> 01:11:59,670
And then, every country has
some other political divide,

1349
01:11:59,670 --> 01:12:01,720
division as well.

1350
01:12:01,720 --> 01:12:05,280
So here, I feel like, we
really need to sort out

1351
01:12:05,280 --> 01:12:07,290
what to do with this about--

1352
01:12:07,290 --> 01:12:11,790
regardless of these,
some of these challenges,

1353
01:12:11,790 --> 01:12:13,170
it is true that--

1354
01:12:13,170 --> 01:12:15,480
I personally don't
have a religion,

1355
01:12:15,480 --> 01:12:19,350
but I respect the
people with a religion.

1356
01:12:19,350 --> 01:12:23,430
And I respect the people with a
different cultural background.

1357
01:12:23,430 --> 01:12:26,910
And we have some
sense of how much

1358
01:12:26,910 --> 01:12:30,510
do we believe that we
should respect each other,

1359
01:12:30,510 --> 01:12:33,640
even though the
beliefs are different.

1360
01:12:33,640 --> 01:12:36,510
So we probably need
to work together.

1361
01:12:36,510 --> 01:12:38,370
And it shouldn't be
just AI researchers

1362
01:12:38,370 --> 01:12:39,390
making this decision.

1363
01:12:39,390 --> 01:12:42,570
By the way, this decision has
to come from the humanities

1364
01:12:42,570 --> 01:12:46,480
at large, which is why the data
sharing actually is important.

1365
01:12:46,480 --> 01:12:49,080
But basically, I think
the current version

1366
01:12:49,080 --> 01:12:54,660
that I have in mind
is that the AI does

1367
01:12:54,660 --> 01:13:00,150
need to understand what sort of
differences are OK differences.

1368
01:13:00,150 --> 01:13:02,490
The fact that people
do have differences

1369
01:13:02,490 --> 01:13:07,980
in certain questions
should be learned by AI

1370
01:13:07,980 --> 01:13:11,430
so that-- there are distribution
of opinions as opposed to one

1371
01:13:11,430 --> 01:13:12,600
